<section class="card">
	<div class="page-header">
		<h1>GL Tools</h1>
		<p class="hint">Use these actions to rebuild GL accounts and run validation checks with full error details.</p>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="card">
	<h3>Rebuild GL Accounts</h3>
	<p class="hint">
		Recreates <code>gl_accounts</code> from staging accounts and runs GL validation checks afterwards.
	</p>
	<label class="inline-label">
		<input id="gl-wipe-journals" type="checkbox" />
		Also truncate <code>gl_journal_headers</code> and <code>gl_journal_lines</code>
	</label>
	<div class="actions">
		<button id="btn-rebuild-gl-page" class="btn primary" type="button">Rebuild GL Accounts</button>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="card">
	<h3>GL Validate</h3>
	<p class="hint">
		Runs all GL validation checks only, without rebuilding.
	</p>
	<div class="actions">
		<button id="btn-gl-validate" class="btn secondary" type="button">Run GL Validate</button>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="card">
	<h3>Convert Transactional Account Numbers</h3>
	<p class="hint">
		After migrating all transactional tables and running <strong>Rebuild GL Accounts</strong>, run this to
		convert legacy Firebird <code>accnr</code> values to the new 4-digit GL account numbers across all
		affected tables and fields (<code>acc</code>, <code>accnr</code>, <code>accasset</code>, <code>siid</code>).
	</p>
	<p class="hint warning">
		This runs automatically in <strong>Step 5</strong> of the migration wizard. Use this button only to
		re-run manually if needed. Running it again is safe (idempotent).
	</p>
	<div class="actions">
		<button id="btn-convert-transactional-accnr" class="btn secondary" type="button">Convert Transactional Acc Numbers</button>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="card">
	<h3>Result</h3>
	<pre id="gl-tools-result">No action run yet.</pre>
</section>

<script src="/public/js/tools/gl-tools.js"></script>
